        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This is a Von Neumann design, so pc runs along the top
to the shared RV5-MEMORY block and inst comes back the
same way. A Harvard-style CPU would have separate instruction
memory instead.
An alternate way to implement a Von Neumann architecture is to 
have a fetch/execute cycle, where one clock tick is spent reading the
instruction from memory and the next is spent executing it.</string>
